==Latin==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|la|set}}

===Etymology===
Perhaps from the old, original form {{m|la|sedum}}, but more probably an ablative form from the root ({{m|la||so-}} for {{m|la||suo-}}) of the reflexive pronoun {{m|la|suus}}, and originally the same as the inseparable preposition {{m|la|sēd}}; properly, “by itself”, “apart”, hence, “but”, “only”, etc.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|sed}}
* {{audio|la-cls-sed.ogg|Audio (Classical)|lang=la}}

===Conjunction===
{{head|la|conjunction}}

# [[but]]
#* '''c.&nbsp;{{smallcaps|ad}}&nbsp;65''', [[w:Seneca the Younger|Seneca]], ''[[w:Epistulae morales ad Lucilium|Moral Letters to Lucilius]]'', [[s:Moral_letters_to_Lucilius/Letter_106|CVI]].
#*: {{smallcaps|non vitæ '''sed''' scholæ discimvs}}
#*:: We learn our lessons, not for life, '''but''' for the lecture-room.<!--Loeb ed. trans.-->
#* '''1522''', [[w:Martin Luther|Martin Luther]], ''Invocavit'' Sermons
#*: [[w:non vi sed verbo|Non vi, '''sed''' verbo]]
#*:: Not by force '''but''' by the word [i.e., of God]
#* '''1804''' Jun 12, ''Oberdeutsche Allgemeine Litteraturzeitung'', No.&nbsp;70, p.&nbsp;1119
#*: [[w:non scholae sed vitae|Non scholæ '''sed''' vitæ]] discendum est!
#*:: We must learn not for school '''but''' for life!

